VALUES ('paper_004_v1_table_12', 'paper_004_v1', 'paper_004_v1_sec_e_2_1', 'table', 'Table 12', '( Scaling Law Model Sizes .) Our model sizes and hyperparameters for scaling experiments. (Model dimension and number of heads applies only to Transformer models.) Params 𝚗 _ 𝚕𝚊𝚢𝚎𝚛𝚜 𝚍 _ 𝚖𝚘𝚍𝚎𝚕 𝚗 _ 𝚑𝚎𝚊𝚍𝚜 / 𝚍 _ 𝚑𝚎𝚊𝚍 Training steps Learning Rate Batch Size Tokens 125M 12 768 12 / 64 4800 6e-4 0.5M tokens 2.5B 350M 24 1024 16 / 64 13500 3e-4 0.5M tokens 7B', 30, NULL, 'renders/paper_004/v1/page-0030.png', 'partial')
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO paper_elements (element_id, paper_version_id, section_id, element_type, label, caption, page_number, extracted_text, asset_object_key, parse_quality)
VALUES ('paper_004_v1_figure_9', 'paper_004_v1', 'paper_004_v1_sec_e_2_2', 'figure', 'Figure 9', '(Right) shows these variants compared to the original (homogenous) Mamba architecture. Interestingly, neither change matters too much. The Mamba-MLP architecture is only slightly worse, and still better than all models except Transformer++. The Mamba-MHA architecture is only slightly better, which is somewhat surprising in light of the fact that many recent works have found that combining (LTI) SSMs with Attention can lead to substantial improvements (Dao, Fu, Saab, et al. 2023; Fathi et al. 2023; Fathullah et al. 2023; Saon, Gupta,', 31, NULL, 'renders/paper_004/v1/page-0031.png', 'good')
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

