INSERT INTO paper_text_chunks (chunk_id, paper_version_id, section_id, sequence_index, chunk_index_in_section, page_start, page_end, content_type, text_content, token_count, char_count, location_confidence)
VALUES ('paper_005_v5_chunk_0010', 'paper_005_v5', 'paper_005_v5_sec_3', 10, 0, 5, 6, 'body_text', 'Priorwork(Merrill & Sabharwal,2023a)hasestablishedstrongupperboundsonthereasoningproblems transformers can solve. Specifically, under standard conjectures in complexity, transformers without intermediate decoding cannot recognize all regular languages. In this section, we show some of these shortcomings can be overcomewith a suitable number of intermediate decoding steps

(and projected pre-norm). Specifically, a linear number of steps enables simulating an automaton. We also show this can be extended to simulate t ( n ) Turing machine steps with t ( n ) decoding steps.', 99, 576, 'high')
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

