VALUES ('paper_006_v3_chunk_0051', 'paper_006_v3', 'paper_006_v3_sec_f_6', 52, 0, 34, 35, 'body_text', 'We conducted a study to evaluate human performance on the testmini subset of the M ATH V ISTA , utilizing Amazon Mechanical Turk (AMT). Each question from the testmini subset was assigned to five annotators, all of whom have a history of completing more than 5,000 HIT tasks and boast an acceptance score higher than 0.99, to ensure the quality of the results. The study comprised five test questions and two qualification questions, which were to be answered within a 20-minute timeframe. The qualification questions consisted of elementary math word problems requiring basic arithmetic operations (e.g., addition and subtraction). Only annotators who successfully answered the qualification questions were deemed eligible for the study, and their responses were included in the final analysis. Additionally, annotators were requested to provide information regarding their

