Multimodal Bard: The answer is (C) . The diagram shows a 3D cube being rotated 90 degrees on each axis. Starting from the top, the first shape is a square. The second shape is a cube with a square missing from the top face. The third shape is a cube withasquaremissingfromthefrontface. Thefourthshapeisacubewithasquaremissingfromtheleftface. To find the next shape, we need to rotate the cube 90 degrees on the z-axis. This will bring the square that is missing from the left face to the front face. So the next shape is the one shown in option (C).

