VALUES ('assessment_ai_paper_008_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_008_openreview_2024_02_11', 'ai', 'model_run_codex_review_paper_008_openreview_2024_02_11', '0.5.0', 'iclr_inspired_due_diligence', '0.1-draft', 'approved', 'Summarizing book-length documents ($>$100K tokens)  that exceed the context window size of large language models (LLMs) requires first breaking the input document into smaller chunks and then prompting an LLM to merge, update, and compress chunk-level summaries. Despite the complexity and importance of this task, it has yet to be meaningfully studied due to the challenges of evaluation: existing book-length summarization datasets (e.g., BookSum) are in the pretraining data of most public LLMs, and existing evaluation methods struggle to capture errors made by modern LLM summarizers.', 8.2, 'good', 'worth_reading_with_checks', 'medium', FALSE, 'report_ready', NULL, 'Codex 会话依据《BooookScore: A systematic exploration of book-length summarization in the era of LLMs》锁定 PDF 中的可定位正文，对五个维度进行了独立暂定评估。总分 8.2/10 由五维等权计算；结论受论文自身实验范围、披露程度和未执行复现实验的限制。', '["正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：Summarizing book-length documents ( > 100K tokens) that exceed the context window size of large language models (LLMs) requires first breaking the input document into smaller chunks and then prompting an LLM to merge, update, and compress chunk-level summaries. ", "正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：B OOOOK S CORE : A SYSTEMATIC EXPLORATION OF BOOK - LENGTH SUMMARIZATION IN THE ERA OF LLM S Yapei Chang Kyle Lo University of Massachusetts Amherst Allen Institute for AI yapeichang@umass.edu kylel@allenai.org Tanya Goyal Mohit Iyyer Princeton University University of Massachus…", "正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：Armed with B OOOOK S CORE , we now investigate the impact of several critical implementation decisions on summary coherence, including the choice of prompting strategy, base LLM, and chunk size. "]'::jsonb, '["评分受以下论文内边界约束：Our work presents the first systematic study of book-length summarization using LLMs. "]'::jsonb, '["How stable are the central findings under additional seeds, settings or datasets?", "Which conclusions remain valid outside the evaluated scope?"]'::jsonb, '["Paper-internal evidence only.", "No experiment or code was executed.", "Originality is not an exhaustive prior-art search."]'::jsonb, '{"experiments_reproduced": false, "accept_reject_prediction_made": false, "external_reviews_used_for_scoring": false}'::jsonb)
