A continuous image x : [0 , 1] 2 → R is part of the geometric C α class (Korostelev & Tsybakov, 1993; Donoho, 1999; Peyré & Mallat, 2008) if it is uniformly α -Lipschitz over [0 , 1] 2 \ { γ } , where the i γ are uniformly α -Lipschitz curves in [0 , 1] 2 which do not intersect tangentially. A function f is i uniformly α -Lipschitz over a domain Ω if there exists a constant C such that for all x ∈ Ω , there exists a polynomial q of degree ⌊ α ⌋ such that for all y ∈ Ω , x

| f ( y ) − q ( y ) | ≤ C | x − y | α . (34) x

We explain how to generate numerically such images in Algorithm 2.

Algorithm 2 Synthesis of a C α image via integration Require: regularity α , Fast Fourier Transform FFT 1: Make a contour 2: Define a 1D filter f ( ω ) = | ω | − α 3: Draw a random 1D C 0 function with i.i.d. uniform entries c ( t ) ∼ U ([ − 0 . 5 , 0 . 5]) 4: Integrate in the Fourier domain to define C = FFT − 1 ( f × FFT( c )) 5: Make the background 6: Define a 2D filter f ( ω ) = ( ω 2 + ω 2 ) − α/ 2 2 1 2 7: Draw two random 2D C 0 functions with i.i.d. uniform entries b ( x,y ) ,b ( x,y ) ∼ U ([ − 0 . 5 , 0 . 5]) 1 2 8: Integrate in the Fourier domain to define B = FFT − 1 ( f × FFT( b )) ( i = 1 , 2 ) i 2 i 9: Make a mask and combine 10: Define a binary mask M = 1 y>C 11: Let x = M × B + (1 − M ) × B 1 2 12: return x', 1066, 3109, 'high')
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

