VALUES ('paper_010_openreview_2024_02_11_chunk_0050', 'paper_010_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_010_openreview_2024_02_11_sec_h_2', 50, 0, 30, 31, 'body_text', 'In Section 5.1, we discussed that we were able to discover attention heads in the GPT-2 model that very closely implemented the nearest neighbours algorithm. In this section, we provide more details about that experiment.

Our methodology for detecting attention heads that directly implement the nearest neighbours algorithm is similar to the one used by Olsson et al. (2022) for finding induction heads. While training the model on the Nearest Neighbours task, for each attention head in the model, we compute a ‘nearestneighbours score (nn-score)’. After every 500 training steps, we provide the model with a batch of 100 examples, each example e consisting of 80 points, i.e., e = ( x , y ,..., x , y ) . The nn-score i i 1 1 80 80 (cid:18) (cid:19) is the attention paid to y for predicting y ( 0 < j < k ) where, j = argmax k − 1 x T i x k is j k i =0 ∥ x i ∥∥ x k ∥ the index of the nearest neighbour of x , averaged for the last 40 points (i.e., k > 40 ) over all 100 k

