VALUES ('paper_012_openreview_2024_02_11_chunk_0004', 'paper_012_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_012_openreview_2024_02_11_sec_2', 4, 0, 2, 2, 'body_text', 'Central to the formulation of consistency models is the probability flow ordinary differential equation (ODE) from Song et al. (2021). Let us denote the data distribution by p p x q . When we add Gaussian data noise with mean zero ş and standard deviation σ to this data, the resulting perturbed distribution is given by p p x q “ p p y q N p x | y ,σ 2 I q d y . The probability flow ODE, as presented in Karras σ data et al. (2022), takes the form of

