INSERT INTO paper_text_chunks (chunk_id, paper_version_id, section_id, sequence_index, chunk_index_in_section, page_start, page_end, content_type, text_content, token_count, char_count, location_confidence)
VALUES ('paper_012_openreview_2024_02_11_chunk_0006', 'paper_012_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_012_openreview_2024_02_11_sec_3', 7, 0, 3, 4, 'body_text', 'Below we re-examine the design choices of CT in Song et al. (2023) and pinpoint modifications that improve its performance, which we summarize in Table 1. We focus on CT without learned metric functions. For our experiments, we employ the Score SDE architecture in Song et al. (2021) and train the consistency models for 400,000 iterations on the CIFAR-10 dataset (Krizhevsky et al., 2014) without class labels. While our primary focus remains on CIFAR-10 in this section, we observe similar improvements on other datasets, including ImageNet 64 ˆ 64 (Deng et al., 2009). We measure sample quality using Fréchet Inception Distance (FID) (Heusel et al., 2017).

Table 1: Comparing the design choices for CT in Song et al. (2023) versus our modifications.

