INSERT INTO paper_text_chunks (chunk_id, paper_version_id, section_id, sequence_index, chunk_index_in_section, page_start, page_end, content_type, text_content, token_count, char_count, location_confidence)
VALUES ('paper_013_openreview_2024_02_11_chunk_0031', 'paper_013_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_013_openreview_2024_02_11_sec_a_6', 31, 0, 18, 19, 'body_text', 'In this subsection we reprove Thm.1b via 3 steps. First, we prove that the latent reconstruction function h ˆ = g ˆ f is, under the consistency of the autoencoder, a diffeomorphism. Secondly, we ◦ restate Prop. 3 of Brady et al. (2023) using our notation. It is a result that locally describes the behaviour of h ˆ , irrespective of the shape of the latent training space. Hence, no proof is required. The third and final step is concluding Thm.1b itself. Lemma 5 (Latent reconstruction is diffeomorphism) . Let f C 1 Diffeo( ˜ , R N ) for ˜ R KM (cid:0) (cid:1) ∈ Z Z ⊆ closed and g ˆ , f ˆ an autoencoder consistent on ˜ = f ( ˜ ) . Then h ˆ = g ˆ f is a C 1 - X ·· Z ·· ◦ diffeomorphism around ˜ (Def.7). Z In particular, for any z ˜ , D h ˆ ( z ) is invertible linear transformation of R KM , continuously ∈ Z depending on z .

Proof. Since f is C 1 in an open neighbourhood of ˜ and g ˆ is C 1 on R N , it follows that h ˆ = g ˆ f ˜ Z ◦ is also C 1 in an open neighbourhood of . Z

