VALUES ('assessment_ai_paper_013_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_013_openreview_2024_02_11', 'ai', 'model_run_codex_review_paper_013_openreview_2024_02_11', '0.5.0', 'iclr_inspired_due_diligence', '0.1-draft', 'approved', 'Learning representations that generalize to novel compositions of known concepts is crucial for bridging the gap between human and machine perception. One prominent effort is learning object-centric representations, which are widely conjectured to enable compositional generalization.', 7.4, 'good', 'worth_reading_with_checks', 'medium', FALSE, 'report_ready', NULL, 'Codex 会话依据《Provable Compositional Generalization for Object-Centric Learning》锁定 PDF 中的可定位正文，对五个维度进行了独立暂定评估。总分 7.4/10 由五维等权计算；结论受论文自身实验范围、披露程度和未执行复现实验的限制。', '["正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：Learning representations that generalize to novel compositions of known concepts is crucial for bridging the gap between human and machine perception. ", "正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：(cid:0) ˆ (cid:1) In this section, we show theoretically how the ground-truth generator f and autoencoder g ˆ , f can be constrained to address both slot identifiability and generalization , thereby facilitating compositional generalization (complete proofs and further details a…", "正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：This section first verifies our main theoretical result (Thm.3) on synthetic multi-object data (Sec.6.1). "]'::jsonb, '["评分受以下论文内边界约束：Extensions of Experiments Our experiments in Sec.6.2 provide evidence that compositional generalization will not emerge naturally in object-centric models such as Slot Attention. "]'::jsonb, '["How stable are the central findings under additional seeds, settings or datasets?", "Which conclusions remain valid outside the evaluated scope?"]'::jsonb, '["Paper-internal evidence only.", "No experiment or code was executed.", "Originality is not an exhaustive prior-art search."]'::jsonb, '{"experiments_reproduced": false, "accept_reject_prediction_made": false, "external_reviews_used_for_scoring": false}'::jsonb)
