A.6 H OW THE PERFORMANCE OF T AB R DEPENDS ON THE CONTEXT SIZE m ?

Recall that, throughout the paper, we used the fixed m = 96 as the context size (the number of neighbors) for TabR. We evaluate other values of m in Table 13. Crucially, the choice of m must be made based on the performance on validation sets (not on the test tests). The results indicate that m = 96 is a reasonable default value.', 500, 1813, 'high')
