VALUES ('assessment_ai_paper_014_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_014_openreview_2024_02_11', 'ai', 'model_run_codex_review_paper_014_openreview_2024_02_11', '0.5.0', 'iclr_inspired_due_diligence', '0.1-draft', 'approved', 'Deep learning (DL) models for tabular data problems (e.g. classification, regression) are currently receiving increasingly more attention from researchers.', 8.0, 'good', 'worth_reading_with_checks', 'medium', FALSE, 'report_ready', NULL, 'Codex 会话依据《TabR: Tabular Deep Learning Meets Nearest Neighbors》锁定 PDF 中的可定位正文，对五个维度进行了独立暂定评估。总分 8.0/10 由五维等权计算；结论受论文自身实验范围、披露程度和未执行复现实验的限制。', '["正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：Deep learning (DL) models for tabular data problems (e.g. classification, regression)arecurrentlyreceivingincreasinglymoreattentionfromresearchers. However, despite the recent efforts, the non-DL algorithms based on gradient-boosted decision trees (GBDT) remain a strong go-to so…", "正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：In subsection 5.1, we used TabR-S with the default hyperparameters (see subsection D.8). ", "正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：Recall that on Step-2 of subsection 3.2, we mentioned that it was crucial that all changes from Step-2 compared to Step-0 (using labels + not using queries + using the L distance instead of the dot product) are important to provide noticeable improvements over MLP on several dat…"]'::jsonb, '["评分受以下论文内边界约束：The following limitations and practical considerations are applicable to retrieval-augmented models in general. "]'::jsonb, '["How stable are the central findings under additional seeds, settings or datasets?", "Which conclusions remain valid outside the evaluated scope?"]'::jsonb, '["Paper-internal evidence only.", "No experiment or code was executed.", "Originality is not an exhaustive prior-art search."]'::jsonb, '{"experiments_reproduced": false, "accept_reject_prediction_made": false, "external_reviews_used_for_scoring": false}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

