Figure 1: ( Left ): The DeepSet-style models only focus on processing the subset S . ( Right ): In contrast, INSET not only identifies the subset S but also takes the identification of V into account, which parameterizes the information that S is a subset of V during the training process.', 512, 2090, 'high')
