VALUES ('assessment_ai_paper_017_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_017_openreview_2024_02_11', 'ai', 'model_run_codex_review_paper_017_openreview_2024_02_11', '0.5.0', 'iclr_inspired_due_diligence', '0.1-draft', 'approved', 'Learning neural subset selection tasks, such as compound selection in AI-aided drug discovery, have become increasingly pivotal across diverse applications. The existing methodologies in the field primarily concentrate on constructing models that capture the relationship between utility function values and subsets within their respective supersets.', 6.8, 'adequate', 'selective_reading', 'medium', FALSE, 'report_ready', NULL, 'Codex 会话依据《Enhancing Neural Subset Selection: Integrating Background Information into Set Representations》锁定 PDF 中的可定位正文，对五个维度进行了独立暂定评估。总分 6.8/10 由五维等权计算；结论受论文自身实验范围、披露程度和未执行复现实验的限制。', '["正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：Learning neural subset selection tasks, such as compound selection in AI-aided drug discovery, have become increasingly pivotal across diverse applications. ", "正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：In theory, invariant sufficient representations can be computed by selecting a representative element for each orbit under the group G . ", "正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：The proposed methods are assessed across multiple tasks, including product recommendation, set anomaly detection, and compound selection. "]'::jsonb, '["评分受以下论文内边界约束：In this study, we have identified a significant limitation in subset encoding methods, such as neural subset selection, where the output is either the subset itself or a function value associated with the subset. "]'::jsonb, '["How stable are the central findings under additional seeds, settings or datasets?", "Which conclusions remain valid outside the evaluated scope?"]'::jsonb, '["Paper-internal evidence only.", "No experiment or code was executed.", "Originality is not an exhaustive prior-art search."]'::jsonb, '{"experiments_reproduced": false, "accept_reject_prediction_made": false, "external_reviews_used_for_scoring": false}'::jsonb)
