VALUES ('paper_018_openreview_2024_02_11_chunk_0034', 'paper_018_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_018_openreview_2024_02_11_sec_d_1', 34, 2, 18, 19, 'body_text', 'where n is the total number of image-text pairs, z ¯ v , and z ¯ t are the i -th averaged visual and text i i representations. As shown in Figure 8a, we can observe the obvious modality gap before training, which separates two modality embeddings, and the default gap distance between CLIP ViT-B/32 and T5 is || ∆ || = 1 . 378 . Although the image captioning objective L (Figure 8b) and the addi- Base cap tional objectives (Figure 8c) reduce the modality gap distance to || ∆ || = 0 . 972 and || ∆ || = 0 . 870 , respectively, the modality gap still exists. In Figure 8d, the modality gap between two modality embeddings is significantly relaxed and the gap distance is further reduced to || ∆ || = 0 . 725 with our assignment prediction objective.

