Figure 3: Selective classification results on diabetic retinopathy dataset. R E V A R shows robust improvement in AUC in both in-domain and domain-shift scenarios (panels (a,b)). Accuracy measures also show similar trends, with large improvements in domain shift conditions (panels (c,d)). Finally, selective calibration error measures (calibration of selected data points, panels (e,f)) show that better calibration is a key underlying factor for R E V A R’s performance. See text for details.

