VALUES ('paper_021_openreview_2024_02_11_chunk_0038', 'paper_021_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_021_openreview_2024_02_11_sec_f_3', 38, 0, 22, 23, 'body_text', 'Empirical cost. Per training epoch, we take around 1.2x the naive baseline’s running time. The total number of epochs required are 1.2x - 1.5x of ERM classifier. This makes the training process on average 1.5 times more expensive. These findings were consistent across a wide range of datasets and ranges of hyperparameters, supporting a modest, deterministic increase in running time. This increase is comparable to some selective classification baselines, e.g., 1.3x increase in epochs for SN and 1.2x for SAT. Note, in addition, that baselines such as SAT and DG only work for a pre-determined budget, and changing budget requires retraining from scratch. We only require a one-time training cost.

