VALUES ('assessment_ai_paper_022_openreview_2024_02_11', 'paper_022_openreview_2024_02_11', 'ai', 'model_run_codex_review_paper_022_openreview_2024_02_11', '0.5.0', 'iclr_inspired_due_diligence', '0.1-draft', 'approved', 'Understanding the interactions and interplay of microorganisms is a great challenge with many applications in medical and environmental settings. In this work, we model bacterial communities directly from their genomes using graph neural networks (GNNs).', 7.0, 'good', 'worth_reading_with_checks', 'medium', FALSE, 'report_ready', NULL, 'Codex 会话依据《Modelling Microbial Communities with Graph Neural Networks》锁定 PDF 中的可定位正文，对五个维度进行了独立暂定评估。总分 7.0/10 由五维等权计算；结论受论文自身实验范围、披露程度和未执行复现实验的限制。', '["正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：Understanding the interactions and interplay of microorganisms is a great challenge with many applications in medical and environmental settings. ", "正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：The datasets contain replicates for some of the settings. To make evaluation simple, we average the results of replicates when included in the validation or test sets. Cross-validation (CV) was performed on 5 train/validation/test data splits with 5 model initialization seeds fo…", "正文可定位证据支持该维度判断：The general goal of this work is to train and evaluate neural models for the dynamics of bacterial communities, directly from their genomes. "]'::jsonb, '["评分受以下论文内边界约束：Our work sets the stage for the application of GNNs to microbial communities. "]'::jsonb, '["How stable are the central findings under additional seeds, settings or datasets?", "Which conclusions remain valid outside the evaluated scope?"]'::jsonb, '["Paper-internal evidence only.", "No experiment or code was executed.", "Originality is not an exhaustive prior-art search."]'::jsonb, '{"experiments_reproduced": false, "accept_reject_prediction_made": false, "external_reviews_used_for_scoring": false}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

