INSERT INTO paper_text_chunks (chunk_id, paper_version_id, section_id, sequence_index, chunk_index_in_section, page_start, page_end, content_type, text_content, token_count, char_count, location_confidence)
VALUES ('paper_031_iclr_2026_proceedings_chunk_0004', 'paper_031_iclr_2026_proceedings', 'paper_031_iclr_2026_proceedings_sec_2', 4, 0, 3, 3, 'body_text', 'In this section, as outlined in Figure 3, we introduce LongHorizonUI, a framework dedicated to long-horizon reasoning for GUI agents. Building upon the LongGUIBench benchmark spanning complex games and general application workflows, our approach integrates three core components: (i) a Multimodal Enhanced Perceiver integrating OCR and icon detection, (ii) a Deep Reflection Decider enabling action verification and adaptive planning, and (iii) a Compensatory Action Executor ensuring robust action execution. The following sections detail each element. The discussion of related work is in the Appendix C due to the page limit.', 117, 628, 'high')
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO paper_text_chunks (chunk_id, paper_version_id, section_id, sequence_index, chunk_index_in_section, page_start, page_end, content_type, text_content, token_count, char_count, location_confidence)
VALUES ('paper_031_iclr_2026_proceedings_chunk_0005', 'paper_031_iclr_2026_proceedings', 'paper_031_iclr_2026_proceedings_sec_2_1', 5, 0, 3, 4, 'body_text', 'In this section, we present LongGUIBench, a benchmark designed for evaluating long-horizon GUI tasks by simulating real-world, dynamic interactive scenarios. The dataset is constructed through synchronized collection of action sequences and screen snapshots, captured by professional testers as they execute predefined test cases across diverse applications and games. All tasks mandate at least 15 steps (mean steps: 22.1). Following cross-modal temporal alignment, the collected action commands and screenshots are input into MLLMs, leveraging structured prompts combined with screen perception algorithms, the MLLMs parse operation descriptions (e.g., “click the search bar”) and extract semantic control annotations, including button functionalities and bbox coordinates. This process generates a standardized intermediate representation with a key-value structure that includes the global descriptions ( task_name ) and decomposed subgoal descriptions ( task_steps{action_ID, action_description, action_type, bbox, image_width/height} ). Finally, manual noise filtering yields a long-horizon dataset containing 371 scenarios.

Gaming Scenarios. Games typically involve complex interactive processes. To this end, we collaborate with professional testers to construct 207 high-complexity scenarios spanning 13 popular games, covering core mechanics such as equipment management and event participation. Each scenario is structured as a long-horizon task chain (19 to 37 steps, mean = 23.7 steps), captured in 4508

GUI Agent- benchmark

