Figure 5: Left : illustration of the parametric variable binding enabled by models with reversal skills. Right : performance on the large-scale arithmetic reasoning task with various branching factors. “(P)”: Parametric Memory. “(NP)”: Non-Parametric Memory.

entanglements apart from scaling . Our findings also provide a concrete example that memory layers can improve generalization , corroborating recent efforts on scaling memory layers that report enhanced performance on general-domain tasks (Berges et al., 2024).', 598, 2987, 'high')
