INSERT INTO paper_text_chunks (chunk_id, paper_version_id, section_id, sequence_index, chunk_index_in_section, page_start, page_end, content_type, text_content, token_count, char_count, location_confidence)
VALUES ('paper_040_iclr_2026_proceedings_chunk_0031', 'paper_040_iclr_2026_proceedings', 'paper_040_iclr_2026_proceedings_sec_a_4', 31, 0, 14, 15, 'body_text', 'We conduct an evaluation of LLaVA v1.5 on the AMBER (Wang et al., 2023). AMBER contains both discriminative tasks and generative tasks. The experimental results are shown in Table 7. Our method outperforms existing methods on both discriminative and generative tasks, achieving significant effects in hallucination mitigation.

Discriminative Generative Method Acc ↑ F1 ↑ CHAIR ↓ Hal ↓ AMBER SCORE ↑ Regular 67.4 71.2 11.6 47.7 79.80 VCD (Leng et al., 2024) 68.1 71.1 9.8 43.8 80.65 ICD (Wang et al., 2024c) 70.3 73.4 8.8 38.7 82.3 IBD (Zhu et al., 2025b) 69.2 72.2 9.8 42.2 81.2 DeFG (Zhang et al., 2025) 70.2 73.0 9.1 39.9 81.95 CICD (Zhao et al., 2025) 71.1 73.1 6.6 34.8 83.25 Ours 81.9 87.2 4.9 20.9 90.01

Table 7: Results on AMBER. The best results are shown in bold.

