VALUES ('dim_paper_040_reproducibility_transparency', 'assessment_ai_paper_040_iclr_2026_proceedings', 'reproducibility_transparency', 'applicable', 7, 'good', 0.2, 'reproducibility transparency', '正文对可复现性与透明度的主要支持为：We validate the effectiveness on mainstream LVLMs: LLaVAv1.5 7B (Liu et al., 2024c) and QwenVL 7B (Bai et al., 2023), and compare DMAS with state-of-the-art methods: ICT (Chen et al., 2025a), AGLA (An et al., 2025), VAF (Yin et al., 2025), VTI (Liu et al., 202；边界证据为：This paper proposes dynamic multimodal activation steering, a training-free approach to mitigate hallucination in LVLMs by dynamically intervening in attention head activations. The experiments on multiple benchmarks demonstrate the effectiveness of our method', '["可定位正文支持：We validate the effectiveness on mainstream LVLMs: LLaVAv1.5 7B (Liu et al., 2024c) and QwenVL 7B (Bai et al., 2023), and compare DMAS with state-of-the-art methods: ICT (Chen et al., 2025a), AGLA (An et al., 2025), VAF (Yin et al., 2025), VTI (Liu et al., 202"]'::jsonb, '["结论范围受此正文边界约束：This paper proposes dynamic multimodal activation steering, a training-free approach to mitigate hallucination in LVLMs by dynamically intervening in attention head activations. The experiments on multiple benchmarks demonstrate the effectiveness of our method"]'::jsonb, '依据锁定评分指南的 1–10 锚点，综合支持证据、边界证据与披露完整度，可复现性与透明度评为 7/10。', 'medium', NULL)
