Results. Some representative task examples and syn- 1.0 Base Policy Finetuned Policy thetic trajectories are visualized in Figure 8, and quan- 0.88 0.91 0.83 0.8 0.80 0.75 titative results are reported in Figure 9. While the e t a pretrained π policy achieves low success rates on r ss 0.6 0.57 0 . 5 unfamiliar objects and novel instructions, post-training e cc 0.4 0.44 0.39 u S aligns the model with new instructions and boosts the 0.29 0.25 0.2 success rate from 38.7% to 83.4% on these downstream tasks. We include task details in Appendix C. 0.0 Spatial Shape Towel-Dir Novel-Obj Average Figure 9: Policy improvement. Posttraining on synthetic data improves policy', 504, 2422, 'high')
