VALUES ('paper_043_iclr_2026_proceedings_chunk_0011', 'paper_043_iclr_2026_proceedings', 'paper_043_iclr_2026_proceedings_sec_3_3', 11, 0, 5, 5, 'body_text', 'The goal of this category is to ensure that a fair machine learning algorithm’s predictions retain minimal sensitive information. L = D (ˆ Y ,S ) , (9) fairness The HSIC and PR in Table 1 belong to this category. Specifically, the D (ˆ Y ,S ) is defined as: PR (cid:18) (cid:19) (cid:88) (cid:88) p (ˆ y,s ) D ( Y ˆ ,S ) = p (ˆ y,s )log . (10) PR p (ˆ y ) p ( s ) y ˆ ∈ Y ˆ s ∈ S Note that, adversarial debiasing methods (Zhang et al., 2018) fall into this category because they employ discriminators to predict sensitive group membership from the learned encoded representations. These methods aim to make sensitive attributes difficult to deduce from the encoded representations.', 169, 681, 'high')
