Figure 9: Combining voting and LiRA does not improve attack performance. (a) Scatter plot showing correlation between LiRA and voting scores reveals low correlation ( ρ = 0 . 27 ). (b) ROC curves for the combined attack and (c) TPR at 1% FPR for different weightings of the two attacks. We show that the combined attack does not improve over voting alone.

where s ( t ) and s ( t ) are normalized to [0 , 1] , and w ∈ [0 , 1] controls the weighting. We LiRA voting evaluate w ∈ { 0 , 0 . 25 , 0 . 5 , 0 . 75 , 1 . 0 } to identify the optimal combination.

Figure 9 shows ROC curves for the individual and combined attacks. The combined method does not improve over voting alone. Since LiRA substantially underperforms voting on Image-based scoring (AUC ≈ 0 . 6 vs. ≈ 0 . 95 ) and the voting-based attack already matches the oracle attack performance (Figure 8), LiRA contributes mostly noise when combined.', 497, 1901, 'high')
