VALUES ('paper_048_ev_007', 'assessment_ai_paper_048_iclr_2025_proceedings', 'paper_048_iclr_2025_proceedings_chunk_0011', NULL, 6, NULL, 'text', 'paper_048_iclr_2025_proceedings_chunk_0011', 'quote', 'Heterogeneous Experimental Setup. We FedTextGrad Table 1: Performance of Heterogeneous evaluate the Heterogeneous FedTextGrad Framework Across Batch framework using three distinct datasets: Object Sizes ( B ) and Local Steps ( E ). This table Counting, Multistep Arithmetic, and GSM8K, presents the performance of the Heterogewith each dataset representing a client in the neous FedTextGrad framework using three federated learning setting. The experiments fodatasets (Object Counting, Multistep Arithmetic, cus on two critical hyperparameters: the num- GSM8K) as clients in a federated learning setup, ber of local steps ( E ) and batch size ( B ). Lowith a total of 3 clients. cal steps ( E ) refer to the number of clientspecific updates performed before global model synchronization, while the batch size ( B ) de- E B = 1 B = 3 B = 10 termines the number of samples processed in 3 0.73 (0.03) 0.', 'high', 'paper_048_iclr_2025_proceedings_sec_3_3', NULL, FALSE)
