Figure 4: The objective values of solutions generated by different approaches across the 100 test instances. “BKS” denotes the best known solutions. “Gurobi” denotes the heuristic module in Gurobi that searches for heuristic solutions before the exact resolution process. For a better visualization, objective values for the instances with no feasible solution found are assigned as 3000 , 300 , and 10000 , respectively on these datasets.', 447, 2031, 'high')
